{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Discovery: Identified from the proteome by analyzing the peptides <10 kDa. Other LGHs do not have activity. Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that the sequence of LGH2 shows 40.9% similarity to frog Temporin-RN3. 20% F; 20% L; 10% P and 10% K. Mol Wt: 2447.951; GRAVY: 0.28; mol formula: C123H181N28O24. Mainly Activity: Active against Gram+ bacteria S. aureus ATCC 29213 (MIC 4 uM), L. monocytogenes ATCC 7611 (MIC 4 uM), L. casei HZ1 (MIC 32 uM) and Gram- E. aerogenes ATCC 13048 (MIC 64 uM). Inactive: K.pneumoniae ATCC 700603 (MIC>256 uM), fungi S.cerevisiae (MIC>256 uM) and P.pastoris (MIC>256 uM). In vitro Toxicity: HC50=50% hemolytic concentration ~40 uM (sheep RBC): moderate hemolytic. Structure: The helical structure observed in 10 mM SDS or 50% TFE can be responsible for the activity and cytotoxicity. Updated 7/2021", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "30177656", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Molecules. 2018 Sep 3;23(9). pii: E2246. doi: 10.3390/molecules23092246. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03013", "source_id": "AP03013", "source_numeric_id": "03013", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03013", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Identification, Recombinant Expression, and Characterization of LHG2, a Novel Antimicrobial Peptide of Lactobacillus casei HZ1.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
